{
  "description": "Implement a Wikipedia Pageviews benchmark using Wikimedia Foundation data dumps.\nThis benchmark provides a high-volume time-series analytics workload based on\none of the world's largest websites, enabling performance testing of temporal\naggregations, trending analysis, and high-cardinality data processing.\n\nWikipedia Pageviews is excellent for benchmarking because:\n- Massive scale: 400B+ rows, 10+ TB across all years\n- Simple schema with high-cardinality string columns (page titles)\n- Real traffic patterns with natural spikes and trends\n- Time-series optimized workload (hourly granularity)\n- Multiple access methods (BigQuery, direct download)\n\nUse cases covered:\n- Trending page detection\n- Traffic pattern analysis (temporal, geographic)\n- Cross-language comparisons\n- Spike detection and event correlation\n- High-cardinality aggregations\n",
